## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates the ability to design systems that support runtime extensibility without downtime—a critical requirement for data platforms at companies like Plaid, Hugging Face, and Apple. It assesses understanding of how design patterns like Strategy, Factory, and Registry work together in live data ingestion systems.

## Key Concepts

- Runtime extensibility through a centralized registry
- Clear separation of concerns between validation logic, orchestration, and metadata-driven routing
- Zero-downtime deployment of new validation rules
- Dynamic validator selection and ordered execution

## Code Example

```javascript
// Core interfaces and registry
class IValidator {
  validate(record) {
    throw new Error('validate method must be implemented');
  }
}

class ValidationResult {
  constructor(isValid, errors = []) {
    this.isValid = isValid;
    this.errors = errors;
  }
}

class ValidatorRegistry {
  constructor() {
    this.validators = new Map();
  }

  register(name, validatorClass) {
    this.validators.set(name, validatorClass);
  }

  create(name, config = {}) {
    const ValidatorClass = this.validators.get(name);
    if (!ValidatorClass) {
      throw new Error(`Validator '${name}' not found`);
    }
    return new ValidatorClass(config);
  }
}
```

```javascript
// Example validator implementation
class URLFormatValidator extends IValidator {
  validate(record) {
    const urlPattern = /^https?:\/\/.+/;
    if (record.url && !urlPattern.test(record.url)) {
      return new ValidationResult(false, ['Invalid URL format']);
    }
    return new ValidationResult(true);
  }
}
```

```javascript
// Runtime registration and usage
const registry = new ValidatorRegistry();
registry.register('url-format', URLFormatValidator);

// New validator can be registered at runtime
class EmailFormatValidator extends IValidator {
  validate(record) {
    const emailPattern = /^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/;
    if (record.email && !emailPattern.test(record.email)) {
      return new ValidationResult(false, ['Invalid email format']);
    }
    return new ValidationResult(true);
  }
}

// Register without broker restart
registry.register('email-format', EmailFormatValidator);
```

